{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>When he tends it.</b> A term of cleaning the lamps of the menorah from the ash of the wicks that burned at night — and he would tend them every single morning." "<b>Its lamps.</b> לו\"שיש בְּלַעַ\"ז, and so all 'lamps' (נֵרוֹת) mentioned in connection with the menorah — except where 'kindling' (הַעֲלָאָה) is used, which is a term of lighting."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {1 "The la'az לו\"שיש appears garbled; likely a corruption of an Old French word for 'lamps' (e.g. lumes/luisernes); translated as written."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:43.525116367Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}